  "content": {
    "title": "Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee highlights: Vols end RedHawks' March Madness run",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 7:26 p.m. ETBe sure to follow USA TODAY Sports' live updates keeping track of all of NCAA Tournament's Friday first round games.PHILADELPHIA, PA — Miami (Ohio) men's basketball entered the day with hopes of continuing its magical season and becoming a true March Madness' Cinderella.Those won't happen.The 11th-seeded RedHawks were unable to keep up with 6-seed Tennessee on Friday, March 20 at Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia, as the Mid-American Conference regular-season champion fell 78-56 in the first round of the Men's NCAA Tournament.\"This loss doesn't take away what we've done all year,\" Miami (Ohio) senior guard Peter Suder said after the game.Ja'Kobi Gillespie led the way for Tennessee with 29 points on 11-of-21 shooting from the field, which featured six made 3-pointers in 11 attempts from beyond the arc. J.P. Estrella added 14 points on 7-of-12 shooting and 10 blocks, giving him the lone double-double of the game.Suder was one bright spot for Miami (Ohio)'s offense, as the senior guard finished with 27 points on 7-of-12 shooting from the field.\"He's the real deal,\" Tennessee coach Rick Barnes said of Suder.With the win, Tennessee will now advance to the second round on Sunday against 3-seed Virginia, which beat 14-seed Wright State in the first of four games at Xfinity Mobile Arena on Friday.USA TODAY Sports is bringing you live updates from the 2026 NCAA Tournament first-round matchup between the RedHawks and the Volunteers. Stay updated here:Stream Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee live with Sling TVHIT REFRESH FOR LIVE UPDATES. Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee live scoreThis section will be updated throughout the gameTEAMS1H2HFMiami (Ohio)322456Tennessee512778 Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee updates, highlights Tennessee beats Miami (Ohio)Behind Ja'Kobi Gillespie's game-high 29 points, 6-seed Tennessee moves into the second round of the Men's NCAA Tournament with a 78-56 win over 11-seed Miami (Ohio). The Vols will play Virginia on Sunday.Tennessee leading comfortably at final media timeoutThe Volunteers hold a comfortable 20-point lead going into the fourth and final media timeout of the second half at 74-54. Tennessee's offense has begun to heat up again, as it has hit 5-of-7 from the field of late. Ja'Kobi Gillespie and J.P. Estrella have 29 and 14-points respectively.Tennessee inching close to March Madness winJa'Kobi Gillespie gets the layup to roll in off the glass, and Tennessee extends its lead to 70-49 over Miami (Ohio). The Volunteers are less than six minutes away from advancing to the second round against 3-seed Virginia.Miami (Ohio) showing some late lifeMiami (Ohio) gets a pair of free throws from Peter Suder and then a fastbreak layup from Brant Byers off a steal, but the hole might be too deep for the RedHawks to come back. Tennessee leads 64-45 with under nine minutes to go in the second half. Antwone Woolfolk hits 3-pointer for Miami (Ohio), RedHawks trailing at media timeoutAntwone Woolfolk responds to a Tennessee jumper with a 3-pointer and it gets the Miami (Ohio) fans — including a member of their viral men's swim team that wears Speedos in the student section — going. The RedHawks still have a lot of work to do if they want to pull off the upset, as the Volunteers lead 55-36 at the under-16 media timeout with 14:59 remaining in the second half. Slow start to second halfBoth teams are trying to get their offenses going again to start the second half, as only three combined points have been scored in the first 3:30 of the half. Tennessee is leading by 20 points.Miami (Ohio) turns ball over to start second halfThe RedHawks get a stop on defense, but turn the ball over themselves on the other end. Missed opportunity for the MAC regular-season champion. Tennessee leads Miami (Ohio) by 19 points at halftimeIt was all Tennessee in the first half, as the Volunteers bring a 51-32 lead over Miami (Ohio) into the locker room at halftime here in Philly. Ja'Kobi Gillespie was fantastic for Rick Barnes' squad in the first half, as he finished with 22 points on 8-of-12 shooting from the field, including 5-of-6 mark from beyond the arc.A positive sign for Miami (Ohio) was finding offense a bit towards the end of the half. The RedHawks finished the half making 4-of-5 from the floor. Ja'Kobi Gillespie extends Tennessee's lead to 18 pointsJa'Kobi Gillespie continues to feel it from deep as he drains his fourth 3-pointer of the first half. It's the sixth 3-pointer of the first half for Tennessee, who now leads Miami (Ohio) by 18 points at 41-23 with 3:14 remaining in the first half. Timeout Miami (Ohio).The RedHawks are one for their last eight from the field.Ja'Kobi Gillespie hits third 3-pointerJa'Kobi Gillespie has been nothing but hot for Tennessee here in the first half. The Tennessee guard gets his 16th point of the first half on a 3-pointer, his third of the half. The RedHawks' offense is still looking for its first field goal in over six minutes.Miami (Ohio) struggling offensivelyThe RedHawks were hanging in there with the Volunteers early on, but their offense has gone cold. Miami (Ohio) hasn't hit a shot from the field in the last 4:47 of the game, and now trail 34-19 with under six minutes to go until halftime.Miami (Ohio) trailing at under-eight media timeoutTennessee is starting to pull in this one as the Volunteers now lead 31-17 at the under-8 media timeout. The Volunteers are shooting 12-of-19 from the field to begin the game.Tennessee extends lead, Miami (Ohio) calls timeoutTravis Steel calls a timeout at the 11:03 mark of the first half after Ja'Kobi Gillespie makes it 23-13 Vols.Tennessee leads earlyThe Volunteers have opened up to a 16-13 lead over the RedHawks. Miami (Ohio) has found some success from beyond the arc to begin out. Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee starting lineupsHere's the starting lineups for both Miami (Ohio) and Tennessee in Friday's first round game:Miami (Ohio)Luke Skaljac (Guard)Peter Suder (Guard)Eian Elmer (Forward)Antwone Woolfolk (Forward)Brant Byers (Forward)TennesseeJa'Kobi Gillespie (Guard)Bishop Boswell (Guard)Nate Ament (Forward)J.P. Estrella (Forward)Felix Okpara (Center) Who is Nate Ament? Where is Vols star projected in 2026 NBA Draft?Ament is one of college basketball's brightest stars at 19-years-old, and enters March Madness as Tennessee's second-leading scorer at 17.5 points per game.After suffering a right ankle injury on Feb. 28 in a matchup against Alabama that kept him out the last two weeks of the regular season, Ament returned to the court on March 12 to play against Auburn and Vanderbilt in the SEC Tournament.USA TODAY's Bryan Kalbrosky has Ament projected as an early pick in the 2026 NBA draft. Miami (Ohio) Speedo-distracting swim teamThe Miami (Ohio) men's swim team has been one of the most unusual sights in their bid to support the men's basketball team's NCAA Tournament run, as demonstrated in the RedHawks' First Four game vs. SMU in Dayton, Ohio.As SMU's Corey Washington lined up for a free throw, the swimming team ambled down the stairs of UD Arena and, dressed as if they were about to compete, arguably caused the Mustangs to miss a game-tying free throw:It remains to be seen whether the Speedos will make a return visit for the RedHawks' first-round game vs. Tennessee. If they do, it will be the second consecutive March Madness game that the men's swim team has attended.What time does Miami (Ohio) vs Tennessee start?Date: Friday, March 20Time: 4:25 p.m. ETLocation: Xfinity Mobile Arena (Philadelphia)No. 6 Tennessee vs. No. 11 Miami (Ohio) tips at 4:25 p.m. ET on Friday, March 20 from Philadelphia.How to watch Tennessee vs Miami Ohio today: What channel is Tennessee vs Miami OH on?TV channel: TBSStreaming option: March Madness Live app | Sling TVTBS will broadcast No. 6 Tennessee vs. No. 11 Miami (Ohio) in the Men's NCAA Tournament on Friday. Streaming options for the game include Sling TV and the March Madness Live app (with a TV login).Tennessee vs Miami Ohio predictionEhsan Kassim: Miami (Ohio)John Leuzzi: TennesseeCraig Meyer: TennesseeJordan Mendoza: Miami (Ohio)Tennessee vs Miami (Ohio) oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Friday, March 20Moneyline: Tennessee (-700) | Miami (Ohio) (+500)Spread: Tennessee (-12.5)Over/under total: 148.5",
